      deepTheory: `<p>Chemical consultation is forensic history plus fibre testing — the service is decided before a bowl is mixed. <b>History trawl (2+ years, ask twice):</b> box dyes (metallic salts and progressive dyes react with lightener — green smoking melt), henna (compound/metallic vs pure BAQ — strand-test distinguishes; never bleach over metallics), keratin/Brazilian treatments (coating alters lift + relaxer compatibility), previous perms/relaxers (overlap = breakage; incompatible sequences like thio-relaxer then bleach need months and tests), medications (retinoids, blood thinners affect scalp tolerance), pregnancy/breastfeeding (avoid strong fumes and new sensitisations; defer major corrections), allergies (PPD, latex, fragrance, persulphate respiratory history — asthmatics need dust-free handling and ventilation).</p><p><b>Fibre analysis quartet for chemicals:</b> porosity (float + slip + drying time — high porosity drinks chemicals fast and unevenly: lower vol, shorter time, fillers, bond care); elasticity (wet stretch — under 20% brittle, 30–50% healthy, gummy/stretch-without-return = do not proceed); texture/density (fine + dense processes fastest; coarse + resistant needs full timing); scalp state (broken, inflamed, psoriatic or sunburnt = postpone — broken skin absorbs chemicals systemically and burns). Previous-colour mapping: photograph and section-map virgin vs tinted vs lightened zones — every zone may need a different formula, and single-formula full heads over history are how corrections are born.</p><p><b>Skin test protocol (allergy alert, 48h):</b> mix the exact tint as for service, dab behind the ear or inner elbow, leave 48 hours without washing off early, read for redness/swelling/itch/blistering — any reaction = no oxidative service, ever with that chemistry, plus GP note. Required for: new clients, new colours, post-reaction returners, and after service gaps (sensitisation can develop silently). <b>Strand test protocol:</b> isolate a discreet subsection, apply the exact formula with weighed ratio, process the full time with heat conditions matched, then read four outputs — achieved level/tone, timing accuracy, elasticity change, porosity change. The strand is a binding predictor: if it fails, the service is redesigned or declined, never 'tried on the whole head'.</p><p><b>Consent and the honest no:</b> the chemical consent states realistic outcome (often staged across visits), exact price, time, maintenance burden and test results — signed. Refusal scripts preserve the client: name the specific risk ('your elasticity test shows the hair would break'), offer the safe alternative ('bond-repair course + trim, retest in 6 weeks'), book the next step today. Document no-gos with the same rigour as services — declined chemical + advice given + retest date protects you if they go elsewhere and return damaged.</p>`,
      deepExtra: `<p><b>Reference — incompatibility matrix (never combine without months + tests):</b> metallic/compound henna + lightener = violent reaction, cut out only; sodium hydroxide relaxer + bleach = severe breakage, grow out first; thio perm + immediate bleach = compromised, wait + test; keratin coating + lightening = uneven lift, clarify + strand-test; PPD allergy + any oxidative tint = absolute never. When history is uncertain or contradictory, the strand test decides — chemistry does not accept verbal reassurance.</p>`,
