      deepTheory: `<p>Relaxers and smoothers permanently rewrite curl pattern by cleaving disulphide bonds — the highest-consequence chemistry in the salon, demanding the strictest discipline. <b>Relaxer families:</b> sodium hydroxide/lye (pH 12–14, fastest, most effective on coarse resistant hair, no mixing — but liquefaction-burn risk and no conditioning buffers); lithium/potassium/calcium hydroxide 'no-lye' (guanidine carbonate + calcium hydroxide mixed fresh — milder scalp feel but calcium deposits dry the hair, requiring chelating/clarifying follow-up); ammonium thioglycolate thio (pH 9–10, gentler, re-shapeable, suitable for tinted/delicate hair — needs neutralising oxidiser like perms); low-pH/sulfite and cysteine smoothing systems (gradual, mild). <b>Keratin/Brazilian-style smoothing</b> (formaldehyde/methylene-glycol chemistry in classic versions — ventilation + masks non-negotiable, regulated/exposure-limited in many markets; formaldehyde-free cysteine/glyoxylic systems milder with softer results) coats and crosslinks for frizz reduction over months — it tames, it does not bone-straighten resistant curl, and it alters all subsequent chemical timing.</p><p><b>Virgin vs retouch mapping (the whole game):</b> virgin — protect scalp with base cream, apply 6–13 mm off scalp through lengths first, then scalp-area last (heat accelerates), smooth with back-of-comb in the direction of straightness, never scratching. Retouch — new growth ONLY, no overlap onto previously relaxed hair (double-processed bands snap — the overlap zone is measurably weaker and shows as breakage exactly at the line of demarcation). Timing is brand-strict (typically 15–25 min); check straightness by pressing a test strand smooth — resistance means more time, mush means rinse now. Rinse 5+ minutes lukewarm, neutralising shampoo (colour-change indicator types show when pH normalises — rinse until the indicator confirms), condition deeply.</p><p><b>Scalp safety engineering:</b> base cream on hairline, ears, nape and any scratch; no shampooing immediately before (natural sebum protects — 24–48h since last wash ideal); no scratching during service (fingernails breach the barrier you just based); client reports burning = rinse that zone immediately, not at the timer. Chemical burns from relaxers scar and litigate — the incident pathway (cool, cover, document, GP/dermatology referral, follow-up) must be rehearsed, not read.</p><p><b>Maintenance architecture:</b> retouch cycles 8–12 weeks (new growth only, forever); protein/moisture rotation by stretch test (relaxed hair needs scheduled protein — hydrolysed keratin/wheat treatments every 2–4 weeks); low heat + protectant; silk/satin night protection; trim 6–8 weeks (ends are oldest and thinnest). Texlax (under-processed intentionally looser result) and corrective transitions (relaxer-to-natural journeys with staged trims) are consultation-heavy specialities — price the plan, not the hour.</p>`,
      deepExtra: `<p><b>Reference — relaxer chooser + timing:</b> coarse virgin resistant → NaOH normal strength, 18–25 min; medium/normal → no-lye regular or thio, 15–20 min; fine/tinted/delicate → thio mild or cysteine smoother, test-strand timed; previously relaxed lengths → never re-relax, retouch only; scalp compromised → postpone, barrier-treat, rebook. Burns, overlap bands and under-processing each have distinct looks — learn the trio and every head becomes readable.</p>`,
      caseStudy: { title: 'The overlap snap', brief: 'A retouch client returns at 4 weeks with breakage exactly along last visit line of demarcation. Your records say "retouch, 20 min" with no map. Reconstruct the failure.', tasks: ['Explain the double-processing mechanism at the overlap band.', 'Identify the record-keeping failures that made this untraceable (map? timing order? check notes?).', 'Write the recovery: cut vs treat decision logic, protein schedule, restyle.', 'Specify the retouch mapping protocol (sections, order, overlap guards) going forward.'], debrief: 'Overlap = previously relaxed hair re-relaxed → band snaps at the demarcation. Recovery: cut above the band where viable, else protein rehabilitation + protective styling + staged trims, honest timeline. New protocol: mapped sections, new-growth-only application with 3-mm safety margin from the line, timed checks, full card — retouches are mapped like surgery.' },
