      deepTheory: `<p>Aftercare is where chemical investment survives or dies — the home routine decides week-6 results more than the salon formula. <b>Wash science for chemical hair:</b> sulphate-free colour-safe cleansers (gentler anionic/amphoteric blends preserve tone + lipids); lukewarm water (hot swells and bleeds fresh colour, cool seals); wash frequency matched to scalp (oily 2–3×/week, dry 1–2× — dry shampoo extends, never replaces); double-cleanse only when needed (scalp first, lengths second); purple/blue maintenance 1× weekly from week 2 (never daily — over-deposit dulls). Clarifying/chelating rotation monthly in hard-water or swimmer households (mineral film dulls and greens blonde).</p><p><b>Protein/moisture rotation by stretch test:</b> snappy breakage = needs protein (hydrolysed keratin/wheat/soy treatments, bond builders, 2–4 weekly on chemical hair); gummy stretch = needs moisture + caution (humectant masks, leave-ins, heat pause); balanced stretch = maintain alternating lightly. Oils seal (argan/jojoba on dry ends) but do not repair — sell them as bodyguards, not doctors. Leave-ins with heat protection bridge wash days; silk/satin night protection + wide-tooth day handling prevent mechanical losses that mimic chemical damage.</p><p><b>Environmental protection contracts:</b> heat (protectant to 230°C always, iron temps by type, weekly heat-free days); sun (UV sprays + hats — sun lifts, warms and fades colour unpredictably); pools (pre-wet + leave-in + cap — dry hair drinks chlorinated/copper water, green blonde is preventable); sea (rinse salt promptly — crystals abrade). Each protection gets a product, a behaviour and a rebooking trigger on the aftercare card.</p><p><b>Maintenance cycles that retain:</b> tint retouch 4–6 weeks, toner/gloss refresh 4–6, relaxer/perm retouch 8–12 on new growth only, trims 6–8, bond/mask treatments 2–4 — all booked before the client leaves, reminded at 48h, followed up with value ('how is the colour settling? send a daylight photo'). Aftercare cards state products + doses + cycles + protection + rebook date; digital photos of the card survive handbag loss. Track rebooking rate per chemical client — below 60% means aftercare isn't being prescribed aloud.</p>`,
