      caseStudy: { title: 'The green pool blonde', brief: 'Week-3 balayage returns green-tinged, dry and tangled after a pool holiday. No protection was discussed at the appointment. Recover the hair and the system.', tasks: ['Explain the copper/chlorine green mechanism + dryness cause.', 'Write the in-salon recovery (clarify/chelate, tone check, bond + moisture plan).', 'Design the pre-holiday protection prescription she should have received.', 'Fix the system: which step in your chemical close failed, and what checklist prevents it?'], debrief: 'Dry hair + chlorinated copper water = green absorption. Recover: gentle chelating cleanse, assess tone (re-gloss if needed), bond + moisture course. Prevention: pre-wet + leave-in + cap prescription with the holiday question asked at every summer appointment ("any swimming planned?"). System fix: protection question added to the chemical consultation card — holidays are predictable.' },
